# pytest JUnit reports. junit-results.xml lands in the repo root on *every* local pytest run,
# because --junit-xml=junit-results.xml is in addopts ([tool.pytest.ini_options] in pyproject.toml).
# The fastsurfer-{quick,unit}test-*.junit.xml names are what CI produces (per quicktest subject and
# per unittest matrix entry); CI writes them under /tmp, but they land here when downloaded from a
# workflow run to inspect a failure.
/junit-results.xml
*.junit.xml
/doc/api/generated/
/tools/debug-helpers
.agentbridge/
.agent-work/
